      "writtenOn": "2026-03-13T16:41:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC this code path does **not** use `SkPngRustCodec` nor `SkBmpRustCodec`.  I think that for PNG that is undesirable, because the new code path doesn\u0027t cover some of the functionality provided by `SkPngRustCodec` - e.g.: handling of CIPC, ICCP, GAMA, CHRM and similar chunks (see [`CreateColorProfile`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.cpp;l\u003d133;drc\u003d62b259bab15f5254e61f05fb1f81d47a2acaadc5)), handling of rotation specified in EXIF chunks (see [`GetEncodedOrigin`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkPngRustCodec.cpp;l\u003d356-366;drc\u003d62b259bab15f5254e61f05fb1f81d47a2acaadc5)).\n\nI am less sure about `SkBmpRustCodec`, because ICO-specific decoding needs to do some things in a subtly different way wrt 1) skipping the header, 2) reinterpreting some metadata like width/height, 3) processing of the \"and mask\" in RGB mode.  Still, maybe `SkBmpRustCodec` can implement and offer an API for doing some of those things?  Probably best to consult with @sergiog@microsoft.com who is much more familiar with `SkBmpRustCodec` than me.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "a8cc847ff8d85fac4b72ad032ccaa5d5d09ca93b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
